{"seq":13,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-sonnet-none-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T22:29:57.618Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"a56d50a082ecefd3b39c810caac5499894d0daa6683e40229bbf6db020189e57","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina Kroll, here is what I found for Kwame's review. I read #coastal-team, #coastal-random, Moss's Coastal digests and the public notes. I left out Pellow Home Living and Saltmarsh.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (Gulf Coast)**\n- **#4419:** the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It is still open. This comes from Moss's cheat sheet.\n  - Moss's 11/2 digest puts #4419 under \"Puget Sound Operations\" as a barge slip 7 schedule sync issue. The two notes disagree, so please confirm which account it belongs to.\n- **PD-8841:** how Pemberline Dock handles chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (Gate 4B). This comes from your 12/8 cutover recap.\n- **Open issue, no ticket number:** chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change (cheat sheet).\n- **Open issue, no ticket number:** a CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map (your recap).\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (Puget Sound)**\n- **Feature request #882:** a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by their warehouse managers (cheat sheet).\n- **No ticket number:** the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering supplied a manual CSV patch (cheat sheet).\n- **No ticket number:** a request for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift (11/2 digest).\n\n**Not found**\n- Neither account appears in #coastal-team or #coastal-random. The only other items I came across belong to excluded accounts (#8812, PD-4821, PD-4824, PD-4827).\n- Moss's notes are digests and a cheat sheet. I found no standalone Coastal ticket log, so tickets filed elsewhere won't be in this list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
